            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative evaluation of subjective dyspnea sensation in patients with various diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Results of examination of 180 patients with various diseases (COPD, bronchial asthma, idiopathic interstitial pneumonia, chronic heart failure, obesity) are presented. They suggest qualitative and quantitative differences between dyspnea sensation that may be used for differential diagnostics of the above conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
